.TH VDR-SUITE-BACKEND-AGENT-COMMAND-ADMIN 8 "October 2026" "VDR-Suite" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
vdr-suite-backend-agent-command-admin \- inspect and administer backend command delivery and provider ownership
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdr-suite-backend-agent-command-admin
.RI [ --database " PATH" ]
.RI [ --backend " ID" ]
.RB ( --status " | " --provider-ownership-status " | "
.B --live-provider-ownership-status
.RB " | " --timer-provider-ownership-status
.RB " | " --recording-marks-provider-ownership-status
.RB " | " --recording-cut-provider-ownership-status " | "
.B --set-native-probe-owner
.RB " | " --clear-native-probe-owner " | "
.B --set-live-owner
.RB " | " --clear-live-owner " | "
.B --set-timer-create-owner
.RB " | " --clear-timer-owner " | "
.B --set-recording-marks-owner
.RB " | " --clear-recording-marks-owner " | "
.B --set-recording-cut-owner
.RB " | " --clear-recording-cut-owner " | "
.B --enqueue-probe
.RB " | " --enqueue-native-probe
.RI [ --deadline-seconds " 30..3600" ]
.RB " | " --replay " COMMAND_ID | "
.B --arm-lost-receipt-response
.RB " | " --arm-lost-result-response )
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a trusted local administrator utility that inspects or changes the
Backend Agent command-delivery and local provider-ownership records associated
with a selected backend in the VDR-Suite Control Plane database.
Its status and provider-ownership-status actions output bounded JSON.
Owner-setting, owner-clearing, enqueue, replay and fault-injection actions
are not read-only.  They can change durable state and downstream behavior.
.PP
The utility is not a public client API or a normal Agent enrollment command.
It is not a substitute for backend authorization or for capability, generation,
provider-ownership and result-verification checks in the runtime.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --database " PATH"
Control Plane SQLite database, default
.IR /var/lib/vdr-suite/vdr-suite.db .
.TP
.BI --backend " ID"
Existing backend identity, default
.BR default .
.TP
.B --status
Read the latest command-delivery summary for this backend.
.TP
.BR --provider-ownership-status ", " --live-provider-ownership-status ", " --timer-provider-ownership-status ", " --recording-marks-provider-ownership-status ", " --recording-cut-provider-ownership-status
Read the corresponding scoped provider ownership and activation state.
.TP
.BR --set-native-probe-owner ", " --set-live-owner ", " --set-timer-create-owner ", " --set-recording-marks-owner ", " --set-recording-cut-owner
Persist a corresponding local provider ownership binding; not a harmless probe.
.TP
.BR --clear-native-probe-owner ", " --clear-live-owner ", " --clear-timer-owner ", " --clear-recording-marks-owner ", " --clear-recording-cut-owner
Clear the corresponding persisted ownership binding.
.TP
.BR --enqueue-probe ", " --enqueue-native-probe
Create a command-delivery probe assignment.
.TP
.BI --deadline-seconds " N"
Probe assignment deadline interval in seconds; allowed 30 to 3600.
Default 300.
.TP
.BI --replay " COMMAND_ID"
Request a replay of an existing backend command.
.TP
.BR --arm-lost-receipt-response ", " --arm-lost-result-response
Arm fault-injection behavior for acceptance tests; never run casually on a
production backend.
.SH SECURITY
Use only within a reviewed, trusted administrator context.  Database writes
can create schema or change authoritative command and provider records;
they require an explicitly approved and recoverable maintenance procedure.
Do not run write or fault-injection actions against a productive installation
solely to confirm that the package is installed.  Enrollment identity,
runtime credentials and technical authorization are separate trust boundaries.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/vdr-suite/vdr-suite.db
Default Control Plane SQLite database.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vdr-suite-backend-agent (8),
.BR vdr-suite-backend-agent-admin (8),
.BR vdr-suite-backend-agent-enroll (8),
.BR vdr-suite-daemon (8)
